msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Today, we released Quarkus 3.12, which among other new features comes with "
"what we called the TLS Registry."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The TLS Registry is an important piece of our security infrastructure as it "
"centralizes the TLS configuration to a single place.\n"
"Some extensions have already been moved to it, some others will follow, "
"together with some additional tooling like commands in the Quarkus CLI."
msgstr ""

msgid "The main changes are:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/39825[#39825] - Implementation of "
"the internal TLS Registry"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/40142[#40142] - Load shedding "
"extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/37900[#37900] - Java Flight "
"Recorder extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/40729[#40729] - Introduce "
"container-image-podman extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/36826[#36826] - Initial native "
"image agent with JVM mode tests integration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/40344[#40344] - Update Spring APIs "
"to Spring Boot 3"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/40745[#40745] - Kotlin was bumped "
"to 2.0"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/40714[#40714] - Enhance MongoDb "
"OpenTelemetry integration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.12, we recommend updating to the latest version of "
"the Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of "
"Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus 3.12."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information about the adjustments you need to make to your "
"applications, please refer to the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/"
"Migration-Guide-3.12[Quarkus 3.12 migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "TLS Registry"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"TLS configuration used to be spread in each Quarkus extension and wasn't "
"exactly consistent."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The TLS Registry changes that and centralizes all the TLS configuration in "
"one place.\n"
"Even if centralized, you can define several named configurations that you "
"will be able to consume in the supported extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Extensions using the new TLS Registry are:"
msgstr ""

msgid "REST Client (the one from Quarkus REST)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Mailer"
msgstr ""

msgid "Redis"
msgstr ""

msgid "WebSockets Next"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"More will come soon and you can also expect more features related to the TLS "
"Registry very soon."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can find more information about the TLS Registry in the https://quarkus."
"io/guides/tls-registry-reference[dedicated guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Load shedding"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Load shedding is the practice of detecting service overload and rejecting "
"requests."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 3.12 comes with the `quarkus-load-shedding` extension, which "
"implements... drumroll!... load shedding."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The https://quarkus.io/guides/load-shedding-reference[Load Shedding] "
"reference guide will help you getting started."
msgstr ""

msgid "Java Flight Recorder"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Java Flight Recorder is a monitoring tool that allows to record events "
"recorded during the execution of a Java application."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While you can use Java Flight Recorder with Quarkus as is, the Quarkus JFR "
"provides some integration at the Quarkus level that can be handy."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, have a look at the https://quarkus.io/guides/"
"jfr[Quarkus JFR] tutorial."
msgstr ""

msgid "Container Image Podman"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are using Podman instead of Docker, you can now use the Container "
"Image Podman extension that is dedicated to Podman."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"More information in the https://quarkus.io/guides/container-"
"image#podman[Container Image] guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Native Image agent"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use Quarkus in JVM and native mode and both are their strengths."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Switching from JVM to native can be a challenge though if you have a complex "
"application:\n"
"while Quarkus takes care of all the heavy lifting for the extensions,\n"
"you might have to tweak the native image configuration for your own classes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is often a trial and error process and given compiling a native "
"executable takes time,\n"
"it can be a long and tedious process."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 3.12 integrates with the native image agent to provide some "
"configuration hints."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The general idea is to run your integration tests with the tracing agent "
"and, based on the execution of the tests, it will determine how to best "
"configure the native build."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For now, this integration is only available with Maven but contributions are "
"very welcome to integrate it in the Gradle plugin."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can find more information about this new feature in the https://quarkus."
"io/guides/native-reference#native-image-agent-integration[Native] reference "
"guide."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that newly generated projects will automatically come with the "
"appropriate configuration in the generated `pom.xml`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Spring compatibility layer aligned with Spring Boot 3"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus has a Spring compatibility layer with some support for Spring DI, "
"Spring MVC, Spring Data..."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This compatibility layer has been upgraded to be aligned with the Spring "
"Boot 3 APIs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kotlin 2.0"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Kotlin users will be thrilled, we upgraded our Kotlin support to Kotlin 2.0."
msgstr ""

msgid "MongoDB and OpenTelemetry"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The OpenTelemetry integration in the MongoDB extension has been improved a "
"lot in Quarkus 3.12."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"So if you're using MongoDB and OpenTelemetry, it is a good reason to "
"upgrade!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus CXF"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus CXF 3.12.0 was released and is now available in https://code.quarkus."
"io/?extension-search=origin:platform%20quarkus-cxf[Quarkus Platform 3.12].\n"
"Check https://docs.quarkiverse.io/quarkus-cxf/dev/release-notes/3.12.0."
"html[Quarkus CXF 3.12.0 release notes] for more information about what is "
"new in this release."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelog of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/3.12.0.CR1[3.12.0.CR1] and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/3.12.0[3.12.0] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

